
==========================================================================
  GENERIC QSwitch — same combinator, every first-order payload A
==========================================================================

  qswitch_generic A f g : Bool ⊗ A ⊸ Bool ⊗ A

  A ranges over first-order payloads. f, g : A ⊸ A can be
  arbitrary endomorphisms; they are implicitly eta-expanded
  into wire-level operations on the A payload by case_hom.

==========================================================================
  PART 1: A = Q  (classical single-qubit)
==========================================================================

  PASS  qswitch_generic Q              id id = id  fidelity=1.000000
  PASS  qswitch_generic Q              f f = id_Bool ⊗ (f;f)  fidelity=1.000000

==========================================================================
  PART 2: A = Q ⊗ Q  (multi-qubit)
==========================================================================

  PASS  qswitch_generic (Q ⊗ Q)       id id = id  fidelity=1.000000
  PASS  qswitch_generic (Q ⊗ Q)       f f = id_Bool ⊗ (f;f)  fidelity=1.000000

==========================================================================
  PART 3: A = Bool  (sum-typed payload)
==========================================================================

  PASS  qswitch_generic Bool           id id = id  fidelity=1.000000
  PASS  qswitch_generic Bool           f f = id_Bool ⊗ (f;f)  fidelity=1.000000

==========================================================================
  PART 4: A = Bool ⊗ Q  (mixed)
==========================================================================

  PASS  qswitch_generic (Bool ⊗ Q)    id id = id  fidelity=1.000000
  PASS  qswitch_generic (Bool ⊗ Q)    f f = id_Bool ⊗ (f;f)  fidelity=1.000000

==========================================================================
  PART 5: sample compilation — qswitch_generic (Q ⊗ Q) CX SWAP
==========================================================================
3 qubits, 6 gates
  X q[0]
  CCX q[0, 2, 1]
  QControlBox q[0, 1, 2]
  X q[0]
  CCX q[0, 1, 2]
  QControlBox q[0, 1, 2]
  perm: [0, 1, 2]

  Compiled successfully. Circuit size: 6 gates.

==========================================================================
  SUMMARY
==========================================================================

  qswitch_generic works UNCHANGED at every first-order payload A.
  The combinator is Q-agnostic; the payload only needs to satisfy
  first_order (no Lolli anywhere). f and g are eta-expanded as
  operations on A's wires by case_hom — the payload never sees
  a function value, so the first-order guard is trivially met.
